From 15156ace56287143960aceea0e7efca1d82cc8ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:10:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the interactive 3D model (GLB) block
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New 'Modello 3D' block for projects.execution, alongside Testo, Media
and Sito live: an upload field for an already web-ready .glb, an
optional poster image shown while it loads, and auto-rotate — rendered
client-side with Google's <model-viewer> (new dependency,
@google/model-viewer). Built for the Oway/Cosmoprof stand model, which
only existed as a 60MB SketchUp file with flat (untextured) material
colors; converting that to .glb and compressing it with Draco geometry
compression (gltf-transform optimize --compress draco) took it from
287MB to roughly 8.65MB with the flat colors intact, verified by
inspecting the material/color data directly rather than visually.

Three things worth knowing about the implementation:

- The custom element is dynamically imported inside useEffect, not at
  module scope: @google/model-viewer calls customElements.define() on
  import, which touches document and would break this (client)
  component's server-rendered pass if imported eagerly.
- src/types/model-viewer.d.ts augments declare module 'react' {
  namespace JSX }, not the classic declare global { namespace JSX } —
  @types/react 19 moved IntrinsicElements under React.JSX with no
  global JSX namespace left for anything to bridge to.
- payload-types.ts was updated by hand, as with the two previous
  blocks: no live database to run generate:types against from here.
  20261002_120000_add_model_3d_block.ts is the accompanying migration
  this time — included from the start, unlike live-embed's first
  patch, which shipped the block without it and broke that deploy.
